-- #556: a HEX literal whose magnitude reaches 2^64 is a lexer error, exactly as
-- the decimal `int_literal_overflow` fixture is.  Before #556 the radix path had
-- no guard at all: `parseRadix` accumulated in the compiler's own 63-bit Int and
-- wrapped silently, reinterpreting a source literal as a different number.
-- Self-hosted reference: integer literal too large for U64 (max 2^64 - 1)
x = 0x10000000000000000
